From 4a531e413fbf5a10ed380ce713318a1a5d727262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Natanael Copa <ncopa@alpinelinux.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:07:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libbb: pw_encrypt(): reject DES fallback from libc crypt()

This problem occurs when BusyBox uses the crypt() function of musl
(CONFIG_USE_BB_CRYPT is off).

"mkpasswd -m yescrypt" gives a DES hash and shows no error. The hash
always has the salt "$y". DES uses only the first eight characters
of the password. The commands "cryptpw", "passwd -a yescrypt" and
"chpasswd -c yescrypt" have the same problem.

The crypt() function of musl uses DES when it does not know the
"$id$" prefix of the salt. A DES hash has 13 characters. All "$id$"
hashes are longer.

function                                             old     new   delta
pw_encrypt                                            33      60     +27

Fixes: 80e676664 ("libbb: add yescrypt password hashing support")
Signed-off-by: Natanael Copa <ncopa@alpinelinux.org>
Signed-off-by: Denys Vlasenko <vda.linux@googlemail.com>
---
 libbb/pw_encrypt.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libbb/pw_encrypt.c b/libbb/pw_encrypt.c
index 93653de..7f51aa0 100644
--- a/libbb/pw_encrypt.c
+++ b/libbb/pw_encrypt.c
@@ -160,10 +160,17 @@ char* FAST_FUNC pw_encrypt(const char *clear, const char *salt, int cleanup)
 
 	encrypted = crypt(clear, salt);
 	/*
-	 * glibc used to return "" on malformed salts (for example, ""),
-	 * but since 2.17 it returns NULL.
+	 * glibc used to return "" on malformed salts (for example, "" salt),
+	 * but since 2.17 it may return NULL.
+	 * musl returns "*" on bad "$2" salts, and a 13-char DES hash
+	 * for unknown "$id$" (e.g. "$y$"): essentially, musl
+	 * uses "$y" as a *DES* salt, even though it is invalid
+	 * (contains chars not in "./0-9A-Za-z" set).
 	 */
-	if (!encrypted || !encrypted[0])
+	if (!encrypted || !encrypted[0]
+	/* '$' salt and 13-char DES result? not ok, should be longer, non-DES result */
+	 || (salt[0] == '$' && strlen(encrypted) <= 13)
+	)
 		bb_simple_error_msg_and_die("bad salt");
 	return xstrdup(encrypted);
 }
-- 
